# Code comments

When writing or editing code, put a **1–2 sentence comment immediately above** any non-obvious block: tricky control flow, workarounds, invariants, timing, caching, platform quirks, or anything a later reader would not infer from the names alone.

Comment **why**, not what. Skip comments on straightforward code (simple returns, obvious maps, standard hooks).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — narrates the next line
// Increment i by 1
i += 1;

// ❌ BAD — no comment on a non-obvious choice
setTimeout(() => flushResume(), 60_000);

// ✅ GOOD — why, placed above the block
// Persist on a 1-minute debounce so cloud writes stay off the playback tick.
setTimeout(() => flushResume(), 60_000);
```
